  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business set-asides obligated $303M in FY2027 to date. The program recorded 1,202 awards with an average award size of $252K. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. Historical obligations show FY22 at $8B, FY23 at $9.1B, FY24 at $8.8B, FY25 at $8.7B, and FY26 at $10B. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying for FY2027 to date with $300M in obligations. The top industries for FY2027 to date include Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $61.2M and Other Computer Related Services at $37.4M. STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC was the largest vendor for FY2027 to date with $19.4M in obligations. The FY2027 to date totals are partial because fiscal year data are reported through the current fiscal year to date only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did SDVOSB obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and $10B in FY26, before reaching $303M in FY27 to date. The sharp reduction in FY27 to date shows a material drop in obligations compared with recent full fiscal years. The FY27 figure is a partial fiscal-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who and which industries dominated SDVOSB set-aside awards in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $300M, making the agency the dominant buyer for FY2027 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $61.2M, followed by Other Computer Related Services with $37.4M. STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC was the top vendor with $19.4M, followed by BLUE CORD DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION, LLC with $13M. The program recorded 1,202 awards at an average award size of $252K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through SDVOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $303M through SDVOSB set-asides in FY2027 to date. The program recorded 1,202 awards with an average award size of $252K; prior full fiscal-year obligations were $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and $10B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use SDVOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs used SDVOSB set-asides the most in FY2027 to date, obligating $300M. The Department of Homeland Security followed with $2M and the Department of the Treasury followed with $1.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors?",
      "a": "STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC was the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractor in FY2027 to date with $19.4M in obligations. BLUE CORD DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION, LLC was next with $13M, and SUPERIOR KEYSTONE LLC followed with $12.1M."
